WEBVTT

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:04.667
A while loop keeps repeating as long as its condition remains true.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:11.112
Count begins at five. Each repetition prints the current count and subtracts one.

00:00:11.112 --> 00:00:18.200
Eventually count reaches zero, the condition count greater than zero becomes false, and the loop stops.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:27.422
Whenever you write a while loop, ask one safety question: what changes inside the loop so it can eventually end?

00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:32.350
If nothing changes the condition, you may accidentally create an infinite loop.
